        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Carved wooden marionette (one of two in this troupe - see also S.280-1999), in the form of a contracting and extending Scaramouche, dressed in the outfit worn by the music hall performer J.H. Stead. \n\nIvory, black and  red painted face and eyes with black dots for pupils. Strongly carved moustache and beard, painted black. Wearing a pointed dark blue hat with yellow dots, and a dark pink and white striped suit, with separate white cotton ruff at the neck, and integral ruffs at the wrists, waist and bottoms of the trousers. Thighs and upper arms each containing two basket rings with run-through strings for contraction.  One ring between pelvis and shoulders for contraction.\n\nTwo control bars;  bar one with five notches, the centre one not in use; two strings to each of the inner notches running through bar two, and to shoulders, arms to elbows.  Bar two with seven notches - two in use on either side of the centre to support the head, and the centre string to the backside for bowing."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/d15824d4-feb3-3cad-8c8d-cd5785fd4182> .

